_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 81
---
order: 81
---
short_label: X.81
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: To a second apotome of a medial straight line only one medial straight line can be annexed which is commensurable with the whole in square only and which contains with the whole a medial rectangle.
----
proof:

Let {AB} be a second apotome of a medial straight line and {BC} an annex to {AB}. Then {AC} and {CB} are medial straight lines commensurable in square only such that the rectangle {AC} by {CB} which they contain is medial. [!just X.75]

I say that no other medial straight line can be annexed to {AB} which is commensurable with the whole in square only and which contains with the whole a medial rectangle.

If possible, let {BD} also be so annexed. Then {AD} and {DB} are also medial straight lines commensurable in square only such that the rectangle {AD} by {DB} which they contain is medial. [!just X.75]

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="200" height="280" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="X.81 diagram" src="propX81.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // Joyce's figure: the second apotome of a medial AB with its annex BC and
    // the rival annex BD (AD drawn whole), and below, the rational line EF
    // with EG (EFGM) applied to it, HG (MGLH) subtracted from it, and the
    // further strip MGIN that completes EI. Added, all invisible at rest:
    // initiallyHidden solid twins AC and BD, so AC stands with the annex BC
    // and BD strokes from B when it is "also so annexed" (Joyce's AD is lit
    // only when the prose names it); an initiallyHidden solid twin EF, set
    // out before the rectangles are applied; transparent targets AB, CB and
    // the breadths EM, HM, EN, HN, EH (;0;0;0); faceless targets EG (E,F,G,M,
    // a twin of the random-faced EFGM, which would be raised over MGLH when
    // lit, #140), EL (E,F,L,H), EI (E,F,I,N) and HI (H,L,I,N). HG / GH reach
    // Joyce's MGLH by alias. No angle is called right, so no markers.
    //
    // Draggables (checked against the bundle): A, B, C, D, F, E (line
    // sliders) and the offscreen frees. D arrives with "let BD also be so
    // annexed", F and E with "Set out a rational straight line EF", so all
    // three are deferred. G, M, L, H, I, N are derived and listed per slide.
    var GIVEN = ["A","B","C","AB","CB","AC"];
    var BDS   = GIVEN.concat(["D","BD"]);
    var EFS   = BDS.concat(["E","F","EF"]);
    var EGS   = EFS.concat(["G","M","EFGM","EG","EM"]);
    var HGS   = EGS.concat(["L","H","MGLH","HM","EL","EH"]);
    var ALL   = HGS.concat(["I","N","MGIN","EI","EN","HI","HN"]);
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
        title: "X.81",
        elements: [
            "A0;point;free;-1000,40;0;0",
            "A3;point;free;1000,40;0;0",
            "F0;point;free;-1000,75;0;0",
            "F3;point;free;1000,75;0;0",
            "A;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,40,0",
            "B;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,105,0",
            "C;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,135,0",
            "D;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,160,0",
            "AD;line;connect;A,D",
            "F;point;lineSlider;F0,F3,40,0",
            "E;point;lineSlider;F0,F3,160,0",
            "G''';point;perpendicular;F,E;0;0",
            "G'';point;extend;G''',F,A0,A3;0;0",
            "G';point;proportion;F,E,A,C,A,C,F,G'';0;0",
            "G;point;proportion;F,E,B,C,B,C,G',G''",
            "M;point;parallelogram;E,F,G",
            "EFGM;polygon;quadrilateral;E,F,G,M;0;0;black;random",
            "L';point;proportion;F,E,A,C,C,B,G,F;0;0",
            "L;point;extend;G,L',G,L'",
            "H;point;parallelogram;M,G,L",
            "MGLH;polygon;quadrilateral;M,G,L,H;0;0;black;random",
            "I';point;proportion;F,E,A,D,A,D,F,G'';0;0",
            "I;point;proportion;F,E,B,D,B,D,I',G''",
            "N;point;parallelogram;E,F,I",
            "MGIN;polygon;quadrilateral;M,G,I,N;0;0;black;random",
            // Slide-only twins and highlight targets.
            "AC;line;connect;A,C",
            "BD;line;connect;B,D",
            "EF;line;connect;E,F",
            "AB;line;connect;A,B;0;0;0",
            "CB;line;connect;C,B;0;0;0",
            "EM;line;connect;E,M;0;0;0",
            "HM;line;connect;H,M;0;0;0",
            "EN;line;connect;E,N;0;0;0",
            "HN;line;connect;H,N;0;0;0",
            "EH;line;connect;E,H;0;0;0",
            "EG;polygon;quadrilateral;E,F,G,M;0;0;0;0",
            "EL;polygon;quadrilateral;E,F,L,H;0;0;0;0",
            "EI;polygon;quadrilateral;E,F,I,N;0;0;0;0",
            "HI;polygon;quadrilateral;H,L,I,N;0;0;0;0"
        ],
        initiallyHidden: ["AC","BD","EF"],
        deferDraggables: ["D","F","E"],
        aliases: { "BC": "CB", "DB": "BD", "HG": "MGLH", "GH": "MGLH", "MH": "HM" },
        slides: [
            { text: "“To a second apotome of a medial straight line only one medial straight line can be annexed",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","CB"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "X.81" }] },
            { text: "which is commensurable with the whole in square only and which contains with the whole a medial rectangle.”",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CB","AC"] },
            { text: "Let {AB} be a second apotome of a medial straight line and {BC} an annex to {AB}.",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AB","CB"] },
            { text: "Then {AC} and {CB} are medial straight lines commensurable in square only",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AC","CB"] },
            { text: "such that the rectangle {AC} by {CB} which they contain is medial.",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AC","CB"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "AB a second apotome of a medial", ref: "X.75" }] },
            { text: "I say that no other medial straight line can be annexed to {AB}",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AB"] },
            { text: "which is commensurable with the whole in square only and which contains with the whole a medial rectangle.",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AB"] },
            { text: "If possible, let {BD} also be so annexed.",
              visible: BDS,
              highlighted: ["BD"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "D",  name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "BD", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeExtend } ] } },
            { text: "Then {AD} and {DB} are also medial straight lines commensurable in square only",
              visible: BDS,
              highlighted: ["AD","BD"] },
            { text: "such that the rectangle {AD} by {DB} which they contain is medial.",
              visible: BDS,
              highlighted: ["AD","BD"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "AD, DB medial, AD by DB medial", ref: "X.75" }] },
            { text: "Set out a rational straight line {EF}.",
              visible: EFS,
              highlighted: ["EF"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "EF", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] } },
            { text: "Apply {EG}, equal to the sum of the squares on {AC} and {CB}, to {EF} producing {EM} as breadth.",
              visible: EGS,
              highlighted: ["EG","AC","CB","EM"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "EFGM", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill } ] } },
            { text: "Subtract {HG}, equal to twice the rectangle {AC} by {CB}, producing {HM} as breadth.",
              visible: HGS,
              highlighted: ["MGLH","AC","CB","HM"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "MGLH", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill } ] } },
            { text: "Then the remainder {EL} equals the square on {AB}, so that {AB} is the side of {EL}.",
              visible: HGS,
              highlighted: ["EL","AB"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "EL = square on AB", ref: "II.7" }] },
            { text: "Again, apply {EI}, equal to the sum of the squares on {AD} and {DB}, to {EF} producing {EN} as breadth.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["EI","AD","BD","EN"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "MGIN", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill } ] } },
            { text: "But {EL} also equals the square on {AB}, therefore the remainder {HI} equals twice the rectangle {AD} by {DB}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["EL","AB","HI","AD","BD"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "HI = twice AD by DB", ref: "II.7" }] },
            { text: "Now, since {AC} and {CB} are medial straight lines, therefore the squares on {AC} and {CB} are also medial.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AC","CB"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "squares on AC, CB medial", ref: "X.15" },
                               { claim: "and their sum", ref: "X.23.Cor" }] },
            { text: "And they equal {EG}, therefore {EG} is also medial.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["EG"] },
            { text: "And it is applied to the rational straight line {EF}, producing {EM} as breadth,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["EG","EF","EM"] },
            { text: "therefore {EM} is rational and incommensurable in length with {EF}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["EM","EF"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "EM rational, incommensurable with EF", ref: "X.22" }] },
            { text: "Again, since the rectangle {AC} by {CB} is medial, twice the rectangle {AC} by {CB} is also medial.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AC","CB"] },
            { text: "And it equals {HG}, therefore {HG} is also medial.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["MGLH"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "HG medial", ref: "X.23.Cor" }] },
            { text: "And it is applied to the rational straight line {EF}, producing {HM} as breadth,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["MGLH","EF","HM"] },
            { text: "therefore {HM} is also rational and incommensurable in length with {EF}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["HM","EF"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "HM rational, incommensurable with EF", ref: "X.22" }] },
            { text: "Since {AC} and {CB} are commensurable in square only, therefore {AC} is incommensurable in length with {CB}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AC","CB"] },
            { text: "But {AC} is to {CB} as the square on {AC} is to the rectangle {AC} by {CB},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AC","CB"] },
            { text: "therefore the square on {AC} is incommensurable with the rectangle {AC} by {CB}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AC","CB"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "AC² incommensurable with AC by CB", ref: "X.11" }] },
            { text: "But the sum of the squares on {AC} and {CB} is commensurable with the square on {AC},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AC","CB"] },
            { text: "while twice the rectangle {AC} by {CB} is commensurable with the rectangle {AC} by {CB},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AC","CB"] },
            { text: "therefore the sum of the squares on {AC} and {CB} is incommensurable with twice the rectangle {AC} by {CB}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AC","CB"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "X.6" },
                               { claim: "sum of squares incommensurable with twice the rectangle", ref: "X.13" }] },
            { text: "And {EG} equals the sum of the squares on {AC} and {CB},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["EG","AC","CB"] },
            { text: "while {GH} equals twice the rectangle {AC} by {CB}, therefore {EG} is incommensurable with {HG}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["MGLH","EG"] },
            { text: "But {EG} is to {HG} as {EM} is to {HM}, therefore {EM} is incommensurable in length with {MH}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["EG","MGLH","EM","HM"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "EG : HG = EM : HM", ref: "VI.1" },
                               { claim: "EM, MH incommensurable", ref: "X.11" }] },
            { text: "And both are rational, therefore {EM} and {MH} are rational straight lines commensurable in square only,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["EM","HM"] },
            { text: "therefore {EH} is an apotome, and {HM} an annex to it.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["EH","HM"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "EH an apotome", ref: "X.73" }] },
            { text: "Similarly we can prove that {HN} is also an annex to it.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["EH","HN"] },
            { text: "Therefore to an apotome different straight lines are annexed which are commensurable with the wholes in square only,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["EH","HM","HN"] },
            { text: "which is impossible.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["HM","HN"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "one annex only", ref: "X.79" }] },
            { text: "Therefore, to a second apotome of a medial straight line only one medial straight line can be annexed",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AB","CB"] },
            { text: "which is commensurable with the whole in square only and which contains with the whole a medial rectangle.",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["CB","AC"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "Q.E.D." }] }
        ],
        resolveJustification: function(ref) {
            if (ref === "X.81") return "#prop";
            return (window.eucrefs && window.eucrefs[ref]) || null;
        }
    });

    // Per-page citation lookup for the slideshow's resolveJustification.
    window.eucrefs = (window.eucrefs || {});
    Object.assign(window.eucrefs, {
        "II.7":     "/elements/books/bookII/propositions/propII7/",
        "VI.1":     "/elements/books/bookVI/propositions/propVI1/",
        "X.6":      "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX6/",
        "X.11":     "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX11/",
        "X.13":     "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX13/",
        "X.15":     "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX15/",
        "X.22":     "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX22/",
        "X.23.Cor": "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX23/#cor",
        "X.73":     "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX73/",
        "X.75":     "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX75/",
        "X.79":     "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX79/"
    });
</script>
</figure>

Set out a rational straight line {EF}. Apply {EG}, equal to the sum of the squares on {AC} and {CB}, to {EF} producing {EM} as breadth. Subtract {HG}, equal to twice the rectangle {AC} by {CB}, producing {HM} as breadth. Then the remainder {EL} equals the square on {AB}, so that {AB} is the side of {EL}. [!just II.7]

Again, apply {EI}, equal to the sum of the squares on {AD} and {DB}, to {EF} producing {EN} as breadth.

But {EL} also equals the square on {AB}, therefore the remainder {HI} equals twice the rectangle {AD} by {DB}. [!just II.7]

Now, since {AC} and {CB} are medial straight lines, therefore the squares on {AC} and {CB} are also medial. And they equal {EG}, therefore {EG} is also medial. [!just X.15; X.23.Cor]

And it is applied to the rational straight line {EF}, producing {EM} as breadth, therefore {EM} is rational and incommensurable in length with {EF}. [!just X.22]

Again, since the rectangle {AC} by {CB} is medial, twice the rectangle {AC} by {CB} is also medial. And it equals {HG}, therefore {HG} is also medial. [!just X.23.Cor]

And it is applied to the rational straight line {EF}, producing {HM} as breadth, therefore {HM} is also rational and incommensurable in length with {EF}. [!just X.22]

Since {AC} and {CB} are commensurable in square only, therefore {AC} is incommensurable in length with {CB}.

But {AC} is to {CB} as the square on {AC} is to the rectangle {AC} by {CB}, therefore the square on {AC} is incommensurable with the rectangle {AC} by {CB}. [!just X.11]

But the sum of the squares on {AC} and {CB} is commensurable with the square on {AC}, while twice the rectangle {AC} by {CB} is commensurable with the rectangle {AC} by {CB}, therefore the sum of the squares on {AC} and {CB} is incommensurable with twice the rectangle {AC} by {CB}. [!just X.6; X.13]

And {EG} equals the sum of the squares on {AC} and {CB}, while {GH} equals twice the rectangle {AC} by {CB}, therefore {EG} is incommensurable with {HG}.

But {EG} is to {HG} as {EM} is to {HM}, therefore {EM} is incommensurable in length with {MH}. [!just VI.1, X.11]

And both are rational, therefore {EM} and {MH} are rational straight lines commensurable in square only, therefore {EH} is an apotome, and {HM} an annex to it. [!just X.73]

Similarly we can prove that {HN} is also an annex to it. Therefore to an apotome different straight lines are annexed which are commensurable with the wholes in square only, which is impossible. [!just X.79]

Therefore, *to a second apotome of a medial straight line only one medial straight line can be annexed which is commensurable with the whole in square only and which contains with the whole a medial rectangle.*

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
